     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" data-account-id=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" accountid=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Andrew Woods</a></p>\n\n<p>I don't think anything further needs to be done for this ticket. With <a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2954\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2954</a> now merged it should be possible for individuals to provide whatever headers they need to in order to support their authz situation. Fedora doesn't define any such headers, so it may not make sense to add specific helpers. The client already supports providing a Link with rel=\"acl\".</p>\n\n<p>So I am inclined to close this ticket if that sounds reasonable to you.</p>\n\n<p>From an earlier slack conversation:</p>\n<blockquote><p>Peter Eichman <span class=\"error\">&#91;2:15 PM&#93;</span><br/>\n@bbpennel I can't really think of anything; it is still all authZ, and the client connection would mostly be concerned with authN, I believe</p>\n\n<p>maybe allowing for custom headers for things like delgate authorization?<br/>\n*delegate<br/>\ne.g., `On-Behalf-Of: someNormalUser`</p></blockquote>",
